items.extend([
('pointEncoding_val','The coordinate equivalence Fin 3 x ZMod n -> Fin (3*n) sends (layer,coord) to the numeric label n*layer + coord.val.',['n is nonzero; layer belongs to Fin 3; coord belongs to ZMod n.'],'Faithful agreement with the existing concrete point labels.'),
('translation_encoding','Concrete translation by g on Fin (3*n) sends the point encoded by (layer,coord) to the point encoded by (layer,coord+g).',['n is nonzero; g and coord are residues modulo n; layer belongs to Fin 3.'],'Point-action correctness, not a seed existence assertion.'),
('translation_val','The numeric value of the translation of point n*layer+coord is n*layer + ((coord.val+g.val) mod n).',['n is nonzero; g,coord belong to ZMod n; layer belongs to Fin 3.'],'Exact modular shift convention used in the existing C19 certificate scripts.'),
('translation_coordinate','The coordinate residue of a translated point is its original coordinate plus the translation residue.',['n is nonzero; g belongs to ZMod n; x belongs to Fin (3*n).'],'Supporting coordinate transport for the freeness proof.'),
('translation_zero','Translation by residue zero is the identity permutation on Fin (3*n).',['n is nonzero.'],'Proved concrete action identity.'),
('translation_add','Translation by g+h equals composition of translation by h followed by translation by g on every point of Fin (3*n).',['n is nonzero; g,h belong to ZMod n.'],'Proved concrete action composition law.'),
('translate_triple_zero','Relabeling a genuine unordered triple by zero translation gives the same triple.',['n is nonzero; b is a genuine triple on Fin (3*n).'],'Supporting identity for actual finite triples.'),
('translate_triple_add','Relabeling a genuine triple by h and then g equals relabeling it by g+h.',['n is nonzero; b is a genuine triple on Fin (3*n); g,h belong to ZMod n.'],'Supporting composition for actual finite triples.'),
('translationOrbit_invariant','A triple and any of its translates have exactly the same full translation orbit, defined as the set of all translated genuine triples.',['n is nonzero; b is a genuine triple on Fin (3*n); g belongs to ZMod n.'],'Discharges hkey for the concrete action; no orbit invariance hypothesis remains.'),
('translationOrbit_fiber','If two genuine triples have equal full translation orbits, some concrete translation carries the first triple to the second.',['n is nonzero; b,c are genuine triples on Fin (3*n); their orbit sets are equal.'],'Discharges hfiber for the concrete action; no completeness hypothesis remains.'),
('coordinateSum_translation','The sum in ZMod n of the three coordinate residues increases by exactly 3*g when a genuine triple is translated by g.',['n is nonzero; b has exactly three distinct points on Fin (3*n); g belongs to ZMod n.'],'Structural sum identity used to prove translation freeness; no seed package assumed.'),
('translation_triple_free','If gcd(3,n)=1, equal translates of any genuine triple under residues g,h imply g=h.',['n is nonzero; Nat.Coprime 3 n; b has exactly three distinct points on Fin (3*n); g,h belong to ZMod n; the two translated triples are equal.'],'Complete general freeness proof via coordinate sums and invertibility of3; specializes to n=19 and29 without enumeration of triples.'),
('c19_development_sound','Seventeen invariant resolved fixed constituents and two resolved orbit-transversal bases on Fin 57 form an LKTS after concrete C19 translation development, provided each realized orbit is owned exactly once.',['fixed : Fin17 -> Blocks57 and base : Fin2 -> Blocks57.','Every fixed constituent and both bases are genuine IsKTS with explicit resolution existence.','The fixed block sets are invariant under the concrete translations on the three19-point layers.','No base has two distinct triples in the same concrete translation orbit.','For every actual triple b, its full orbit set belongs to exactly one input owner among the17 fixed constituents and2 bases.'], 'Conditional seed-package criterion for order57. The concrete action, its orbit invariance/completeness/freeness and17+2*19=55 are proved in the kernel. No compatible seed package or LKTS57 certificate is asserted.'),
('c29_development_sound','Twenty-seven invariant resolved fixed constituents and two resolved orbit-transversal bases on Fin 87 form an LKTS after concrete C29 translation development, provided each realized orbit is owned exactly once.',['fixed : Fin27 -> Blocks87 and base : Fin2 -> Blocks87.','Every fixed constituent and both bases are genuine IsKTS with explicit resolution existence.','The fixed block sets are invariant under the concrete translations on the three29-point layers.','No base has two distinct triples in the same concrete translation orbit.','For every actual triple b, its full orbit set belongs to exactly one input owner among the27 fixed constituents and2 bases.'], 'Conditional seed-package criterion for the surviving27+29+29 order87 pattern. The concrete action, its orbit invariance/completeness/freeness and27+2*29=85 are proved in the kernel. No seed package or LKTS87 certificate is asserted.')
])
